From 20d9fc43bc914c4d270c26776aec7cf6a423c5f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuya Fujiwara <hzw1258@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 22:43:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] Add bare_space_halfwidth setting for Empty Hiragana
 mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce a new `keys.bare_space_halfwidth` configuration option that,
when enabled, makes the bare Space key in Empty Hiragana mode commit a
half-width ASCII space instead of the full-width U+3000. This provides
an alternative to the Japanese-IME convention while keeping full-width
space accessible via Ctrl+Space.

The setting defaults to OFF, preserving the current Japanese-IME
behavior. When enabled, it applies only to Empty state; Space during
Composing continues to trigger conversion mode.

Wire the setting through KeysSettings → EngineConfig → input.rs, update
default.toml and README with documentation, and add comprehensive tests
covering the default behavior and both single and consecutive spaces with
the flag enabled.
